    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/u7DJxTmuY-PRriQ_WqzP3NpTSxNbz31Yer_aINc-e1s.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$x_{1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{2}, x_{2}=\\mathrm{L}, x_{3}=\\frac{5 \\mathrm{~L}}{4}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore x_{\\mathrm{CM}}=\\frac{m_{1} x_{1}+m_{2} x_{2}+m_{3} x_{3}}{m_{1}+m_{2}+m_{3}}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{\\mathrm{M} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{2}+\\mathrm{M} \\times \\mathrm{L}+\\mathrm{M} \\times \\frac{5 \\mathrm{~L}}{4}}{\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{M}+\\mathrm{M}}=\\frac{11 \\mathrm{~L}}{12}$",
